return {["commands"]={["mobs"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Open the console and browse the dashboard or searchable help. Copy exact command syntax; replace placeholders and omit brackets.",["examples"]={"mobs","mobs.help construction","help region"},["notes"]="help is an alias for mobs.help. mobs uses exact command matching when dispatching actions; typo matches only suggest.",["related"]={"find","advice","tutorial"}},["mobs.help"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Open the console and browse the dashboard or searchable help. Copy exact command syntax; replace placeholders and omit brackets.",["examples"]={"mobs","mobs.help construction","help region"},["notes"]="help is an alias for mobs.help. mobs uses exact command matching when dispatching actions; typo matches only suggest.",["related"]={"find","advice","tutorial"}},["mobs.advice"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Use the dotted shortcut or give a command name after mobs.advice. Both display the same detailed guide without executing the command.",["examples"]={"mobs.advice.pile","mobs.advice spawn_resource","mobs.advice.soil"},["notes"]="Each guide includes targeting, steps, examples, limits and related tools. Advice works at the main menu.",["related"]={"tutorial","usage","find"}},["mobs.tutorial"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Read the chapter list, choose a chapter number/name, or print the full tutorial. Examples are explanatory text, never replayed automatically.",["examples"]={"mobs.tutorial","mobs.tutorial all","mobs.tutorial resources"},["notes"]="The full tutorial is long; use the numbered chapters or the linked GitHub wiki when console history is hard to read.",["related"]={"advice","help"}},["mobs.find"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Type several ordinary words or a misspelled command name. Read the ranked suggestions, then enter the exact desired command.",["examples"]={"mobs.find finish buildings","mobs.find fish","mobs.find fertility"},["notes"]="Search never executes guessed commands. Use advice on a suggested command to learn its full workflow.",["related"]={"advice","help","complete"}},["mobs.usage"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Supply a short command name to read its syntax and targeting summary. For a fuller guide, use mobs.advice.<command>.",["examples"]={"mobs.usage pile","mobs.usage spawn_deposit"},["notes"]="Required arguments use angle brackets; optional arguments use square brackets. Do not type either bracket.",["related"]={"advice","tutorial"}},["mobs.complete"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Supply a partial command or a full command followed by a partial argument. The result is text you can copy; it does not run it.",["examples"]={"mobs.complete mobs.sp","mobs.complete pile br","mobs.complete give 17 20 p"},["notes"]="Broad prefixes show command names. Item IDs/names appear after a complete item-taking command. Suggestions are capped in the printed result.",["related"]={"autocomplete","find"}},["mobs.autocomplete"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Load a settlement, open the console and refresh. Type mobs. and use Tab. Fully enter an item-taking command to see item variants. Enter runs the typed command.",["examples"]={"mobs.autocomplete refresh","mobs.autocomplete off","mobs.autocomplete status"},["notes"]="Opening Development once loads card names for completion. Native dropdown support targets 0.8.117; mobs.complete remains available if native refresh fails. Off lasts until the mod reloads.",["related"]={"complete","find"}},["mobs.recent"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Show the most recent successful command strings without replaying them. Choose 1 to 30 entries.",["examples"]={"mobs.recent","mobs.recent 30"},["notes"]="History clears on mod reload. An armed click command being listed does not prove that its later placement succeeded.",["related"]={"status","cancel"}},["mobs.version"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Run without arguments. Read the returned mod/version/context information before reporting a problem.",["examples"]={"mobs.version"},["notes"]="ping proves the command handler responds. is_in_game/debug_task validate context only. They do not test gameplay features or assign worker jobs.",["related"]={"tutorial","advice"}},["mobs.ping"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Run without arguments. Read the returned mod/version/context information before reporting a problem.",["examples"]={"mobs.ping"},["notes"]="ping proves the command handler responds. is_in_game/debug_task validate context only. They do not test gameplay features or assign worker jobs.",["related"]={"tutorial","advice"}},["mobs.is_in_game"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Run without arguments. Read the returned mod/version/context information before reporting a problem.",["examples"]={"mobs.is_in_game"},["notes"]="ping proves the command handler responds. is_in_game/debug_task validate context only. They do not test gameplay features or assign worker jobs.",["related"]={"tutorial","advice"}},["mobs.debug_task"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Run without arguments. Read the returned mod/version/context information before reporting a problem.",["examples"]={"mobs.debug_task"},["notes"]="ping proves the command handler responds. is_in_game/debug_task validate context only. They do not test gameplay features or assign worker jobs.",["related"]={"tutorial","advice"}},["mobs.regions"]={["target"]="Loaded settlement.",["steps"]="List owned region IDs and names. Choose one for mobs.region and check the pin with mobs.status.",["examples"]={"mobs.regions"},["notes"]="Region IDs depend on the save; item IDs cannot be used as region IDs.",["related"]={"region","status","map_regions"}},["mobs.map_regions"]={["target"]="Loaded map.",["steps"]="List all map region IDs, including unclaimed and foreign regions, for map/claim operations.",["examples"]={"mobs.map_regions"},["notes"]="Listing a region does not make it owned or allow ordinary resource edits there.",["related"]={"claim","regions"}},["mobs.region"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Use a real ID from mobs.regions. current pins the camera region; selected pins the selected map region; auto clears a pin. No argument reports the target.",["examples"]={"mobs.region current","mobs.region selected","mobs.region auto","mobs.region"},["notes"]="A pin changes command targeting, not map ownership, camera position or building selection. Numeric IDs must come from your own save.",["related"]={"regions","status"}},["mobs.status"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Run without arguments to see treasury, influence and the chosen owned region with its wealth and approval.",["examples"]={"mobs.status"},["notes"]="If no owned region can be resolved, choose one using mobs.regions and mobs.region.",["related"]={"region","regions"}},["mobs.treasury"]={["target"]="Your player lord; no building selection required.",["steps"]="Use add for a relative change or set for an exact final value. Read the result and mobs.status afterwards.",["examples"]={"mobs.treasury add 1000","mobs.treasury set 5000"},["notes"]="mobs.undo restores the latest economy edit only while the value and player are unchanged.",["related"]={"undo","status"}},["mobs.influence"]={["target"]="Your player lord; no building selection required.",["steps"]="Use add for a relative change or set for an exact final value. Read the result and mobs.status afterwards.",["examples"]={"mobs.influence add 1000","mobs.influence set 5000"},["notes"]="mobs.undo restores the latest economy edit only while the value and player are unchanged.",["related"]={"undo","status"}},["mobs.wealth"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Use add for a relative change or set for an exact final value. Read the result and mobs.status afterwards.",["examples"]={"mobs.wealth add 1000","mobs.wealth set 5000"},["notes"]="mobs.undo restores the latest economy edit only while the value and player are unchanged.",["related"]={"undo","status"}},["mobs.approval"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Use add for a relative change or set for an exact final value. Read the result and mobs.status afterwards.",["examples"]={"mobs.approval add 5","mobs.approval set 80"},["notes"]="Approval must end between 0 and 100 and the game may recalculate it. mobs.undo restores the latest economy edit only while the value and player are unchanged.",["related"]={"undo","status"}},["mobs.undo"]={["target"]="Latest economy edit in this mod session.",["steps"]="Run after treasury, influence, wealth or approval edits to restore the previous value.",["examples"]={"mobs.treasury add 100","mobs.undo"},["notes"]="This is not universal undo. It refuses to overwrite newer simulation changes and does not restore inventory, demolished buildings or spawned resources.",["related"]={"status","undo_resources","undo_soil"}},["mobs.items"]={["target"]="Loaded game item table.",["steps"]="Search by display name or numeric ID. Copy a returned ID into pile, give or inventory commands. Names with spaces can be normalized, but an ID avoids ambiguity.",["examples"]={"mobs.items bread","mobs.items 17","mobs.items"},["notes"]="The wiki lists the full EItemType enum, including recipes/internal values. mobs.items lists the deliverable subset. Enum labels are not always localized command-name aliases. Livestock use mobs.animal.",["related"]={"pile","give","inventory"}},["mobs.pile"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing.",["steps"]="Find an item with mobs.items. Run pile with its name or ID and an amount. Close the console and place the native Supplies preview. Read the delivery result.",["examples"]={"mobs.pile 17 100","mobs.pile bread 100"},["notes"]="Creates a NEW pile. Inventory changes only after placement succeeds. Amount is 1..10000. No preview argument or undo. Use drop to fill an existing target.",["related"]={"drop","clear_empty_piles","remove_selected_piles"}},["mobs.drop"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing.",["steps"]="Choose a deliverable item and amount, close the console and click owned storage, a Supplies pile or a construction site needing that material. No arguments shows pending status.",["examples"]={"mobs.drop 17 20","mobs.drop bread 100","mobs.drop"},["notes"]="Does not create ground piles. Construction deliveries are capped to missing materials including incoming goods. Ineligible clicks leave delivery armed; check the message. No undo.",["related"]={"pile","give","construction_needs","cancel"}},["mobs.give"]={["target"]="Select the owned building in the normal game view BEFORE opening the console. A pinned region does not select buildings. Up to 32 buildings only where the command explicitly allows a batch.",["steps"]="Run with an item ID/name and per-building amount. Preview the exact selection first; remove preview to apply. Every target is checked before the first write.",["examples"]={"mobs.give 17 20 preview","mobs.give 17 20"},["notes"]="Amount is per selected building, not a shared total. give accepts storage/piles/sites. inventory_add also accepts production/housing and bypasses completed-building storage caps. Construction receives only needed materials. No undo.",["related"]={"drop","items","inventory"}},["mobs.inventory_add"]={["target"]="Select the owned building in the normal game view BEFORE opening the console. A pinned region does not select buildings. Up to 32 buildings only where the command explicitly allows a batch.",["steps"]="Run with an item ID/name and per-building amount. Preview the exact selection first; remove preview to apply. Every target is checked before the first write.",["examples"]={"mobs.inventory_add 17 20 preview"},["notes"]="Amount is per selected building, not a shared total. give accepts storage/piles/sites. inventory_add also accepts production/housing and bypasses completed-building storage caps. Construction receives only needed materials. No undo.",["related"]={"drop","items","inventory"}},["mobs.inventory"]={["target"]="Select the owned building in the normal game view BEFORE opening the console. A pinned region does not select buildings. Up to 32 buildings only where the command explicitly allows a batch.",["steps"]="Select exactly ONE owned building, reopen the console, then inspect it. inventory optionally filters goods by name or ID.",["examples"]={"mobs.inventory","mobs.inventory 17"},["notes"]="Building inventory is local storage, not the total regional stock. An inventory_add result may not appear in the top resource bar immediately.",["related"]={"stock","give","construction_needs"}},["mobs.building"]={["target"]="Select the owned building in the normal game view BEFORE opening the console. A pinned region does not select buildings. Up to 32 buildings only where the command explicitly allows a batch.",["steps"]="Select exactly ONE owned building, reopen the console, then inspect it. inventory optionally filters goods by name or ID.",["examples"]={"mobs.building"},["notes"]="Building inventory is local storage, not the total regional stock. An inventory_add result may not appear in the top resource bar immediately.",["related"]={"stock","give","construction_needs"}},["mobs.stock"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Read the target region stock, optionally filtering by item name or ID.",["examples"]={"mobs.stock","mobs.stock planks"},["notes"]="The native regional stock query can include reserved goods. It differs from a selected building inventory. Read-only.",["related"]={"inventory","items"}},["mobs.clear_empty_piles"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Preview the count, then run without preview to remove only confirmed-empty owned Supplies piles in the target region.",["examples"]={"mobs.clear_empty_piles preview","mobs.clear_empty_piles"},["notes"]="Non-empty and unreadable piles are retained. Other regions and buildings are untouched. Removal has no undo.",["related"]={"remove_selected_piles","pile"}},["mobs.remove_selected_piles"]={["target"]="Select the owned building in the normal game view BEFORE opening the console. A pinned region does not select buildings. Up to 32 buildings only where the command explicitly allows a batch.",["steps"]="Select the bugged Supplies pile(s), preview, then remove preview to delete those selected piles.",["examples"]={"mobs.remove_selected_piles preview","mobs.remove_selected_piles"},["notes"]="Deletes CONTENTS as well as the pile, including unfinished/bugged piles. It ignores the region pin and rejects foreign targets. There is no undo.",["related"]={"clear_empty_piles","pile"}},["mobs.cancel"]={["target"]="Any pending one-shot click tool or queued forestry batch.",["steps"]="Run before switching click tools or when you no longer want to place/deliver anything.",["examples"]={"mobs.cancel"},["notes"]="Stops future clicks/batches only. Completed placements, deliveries and growth are retained. It is not undo.",["related"]={"drop","pile","resource"}},["mobs.finish_constructions"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Preview unfinished sites, run without preview, then resume simulation. Watch sites finalize; workers may still need to reach them.",["examples"]={"mobs.finish_constructions preview","mobs.finish_constructions","mobs.speed 1"},["notes"]="Prepares native construction work and supplies missing materials. It does not forcibly replace actors or guarantee instant simulation finalization. No undo; inspect failures in the result.",["related"]={"construction_needs","supply_construction","instant_build"}},["mobs.construction_needs"]={["target"]="Select the owned building in the normal game view BEFORE opening the console. A pinned region does not select buildings. Up to 32 buildings only where the command explicitly allows a batch.",["steps"]="Select one construction site for a detailed bill, or request region totals without a building selection.",["examples"]={"mobs.construction_needs","mobs.construction_needs region"},["notes"]="Required, stored and incoming goods are counted separately. Missing amounts include incoming deliveries to avoid oversupply. Read-only.",["related"]={"supply_construction","finish_constructions"}},["mobs.supply_construction"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin. Use selected explicitly to operate on selected owned sites instead.",["steps"]="Preview first. The default supplies missing materials across the target region; selected limits it to selected unfinished/upgrading buildings.",["examples"]={"mobs.supply_construction preview","mobs.supply_construction selected preview","mobs.supply_construction selected"},["notes"]="Supplies materials only; it does not finish work. All selected targets must be valid sites. No undo.",["related"]={"finish_constructions","construction_needs"}},["mobs.construction"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Use pause or resume to change unfinished sites throughout the target region.",["examples"]={"mobs.construction pause","mobs.construction resume"},["notes"]="This affects the sites construction state, not the global simulation speed. It does not fill materials or finish work.",["related"]={"finish_constructions","speed"}},["mobs.instant_build"]={["target"]="Global native setting for this session, affecting newly placed buildings.",["steps"]="Read status, switch on, place the intended new building, then switch off when finished.",["examples"]={"mobs.instant_build status","mobs.instant_build on preview","mobs.instant_build on","mobs.instant_build off"},["notes"]="Applies globally until disabled, not just in a pinned region. Existing unfinished sites use finish_constructions instead. A restart resets session-only behavior.",["related"]={"finish_constructions","construction"}},["mobs.demolish"]={["target"]="Select the owned building in the normal game view BEFORE opening the console. A pinned region does not select buildings. Up to 32 buildings only where the command explicitly allows a batch.",["steps"]="Select owned buildings, preview the targets, then run without preview to request the native demolition with normal refunds.",["examples"]={"mobs.demolish selected preview","mobs.demolish selected"},["notes"]="Maximum 32 targets. All must be eligible before the first demolition. No undo; already completed demolitions remain if a later target changes.",["related"]={"remove_selected_piles","building"}},["mobs.resources"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Inspect existing clumps with resources. Refill returns matching existing clumps to capacity; empty sets matching amounts to zero while retaining actors. Preview either mutation first.",["examples"]={"mobs.resources berries"},["notes"]="Kinds: iron, clay, salt, stone, berries, mushrooms, fish, eel; wildlife excluded. Does not create nodes or fill storehouses. Existing underground reserves use deposit. Empty seasonal resources may later regrow under game rules.",["related"]={"undo_resources","spawn_resource","deposit"}},["mobs.refill_resources"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Inspect existing clumps with resources. Refill returns matching existing clumps to capacity; empty sets matching amounts to zero while retaining actors. Preview either mutation first.",["examples"]={"mobs.refill_resources berries preview","mobs.refill_resources berries"},["notes"]="Kinds: iron, clay, salt, stone, berries, mushrooms, fish, eel; wildlife excluded. Does not create nodes or fill storehouses. Existing underground reserves use deposit. Empty seasonal resources may later regrow under game rules.",["related"]={"undo_resources","spawn_resource","deposit"}},["mobs.empty_resources"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Inspect existing clumps with resources. Refill returns matching existing clumps to capacity; empty sets matching amounts to zero while retaining actors. Preview either mutation first.",["examples"]={"mobs.empty_resources fish preview"},["notes"]="Kinds: iron, clay, salt, stone, berries, mushrooms, fish, eel; wildlife excluded. Does not create nodes or fill storehouses. Existing underground reserves use deposit. Empty seasonal resources may later regrow under game rules.",["related"]={"undo_resources","spawn_resource","deposit"}},["mobs.undo_resources"]={["target"]="Latest unchanged resource refill/empty batch in this session.",["steps"]="Run after a refill/empty batch to restore its previous clump amounts.",["examples"]={"mobs.refill_resources berries","mobs.undo_resources"},["notes"]="Up to five batches retained. If harvesting or another edit changed any target, undo refuses to overwrite it. It cannot undo spawning/removal.",["related"]={"refill_resources","empty_resources"}},["mobs.spawn_resource"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing.",["steps"]="Choose a supported kind. Optionally give amount PER clump and a clump count, then rich. Preview uses the same click workflow; run again without preview to place.",["examples"]={"mobs.spawn_resource berries 100 4 preview","mobs.spawn_resource berries 100 4","mobs.spawn_resource iron 1000 1 rich","mobs.spawn_resource eel 400 1"},["notes"]="Kinds: iron, clay, salt, stone, berries, mushrooms, fish, eel. Count 1..64; amount 1..1000000 per clump. Fish/eel need suitable reachable water. The 0.16 alpha preserves native aquatic identity/seasonality and adds region availability tags; harvesting and save/load still need testing. Use repair_fishing for existing shoals. Deer/hares use spawn_wildlife instead. No undo.",["related"]={"resource","refresh_resource_icons","pond_fish","animal","repair_fishing","spawn_wildlife"}},["mobs.resource"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing.",["steps"]="Choose an action, kind and an amount only for add. Click near the actual clump/node within 2500 game units. Preview each placement/removal/edit before applying.",["examples"]={"mobs.resource add berries 100 preview","mobs.resource rich iron","mobs.resource refresh berries preview","mobs.resource remove eel preview","mobs.resource remove eel"},["notes"]="remove deletes a whole surface group; remove_clump only one clump. Exact kind is required: fish and eel differ. refresh repairs land clump size/height/visibility, not amounts. Real underground reserves use remove_deposit; empty clumpless non-wildlife nodes are removable here. No undo.",["related"]={"resources","remove_deposit","refresh_resource_icons","repair_fishing"}},["mobs.refresh_resource_icons"]={["target"]="Current game HUD; no click or building selection.",["steps"]="Run preview to compare node counts and count owned mineral render actors that would be hidden, then run normally. This synchronizes HUD icons/hover data and suppresses leaked underground paper-map projections and extra mineral meshes. No click required. An automatic visual repair also runs shortly after loading a settlement.",["examples"]={"mobs.refresh_resource_icons preview","mobs.refresh_resource_icons"},["notes"]="Keeps the separate normal-map icons, paper-map icons and tooltips. Only rendering of owned iron/clay/salt reserve/data actors is hidden: amounts, richness, capacity, node membership and collision/mining data are unchanged. Surface stones and foreign deposits are untouched. Preview changes nothing. It does not repair worker reachability. The manual repair and automatic reload pass cover deposits made by older Mobs candidates.",["related"]={"spawn_deposit","resource","remove_deposit"}},["mobs.spawn_deposit"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console and move the cursor over owned land. A native ground-material preview, centre crosshair and mining-radius ring follow the cursor. Read green READY / red BLOCKED, then left-click the centre you want. Right-click or mobs.cancel cancels; five-minute expiry. Add preview for a read-only tool that stays active across clicks.",["steps"]="Choose iron, clay or salt, an amount and optional rich. The tool uses the game native mineral Blueprint classes and underground-deposit factory; it keeps your click X/Y and snaps only height to terrain. The ring uses the native mining radius: 20m normal or 25m rich on the supported build. A valid click creates one finite surface clump, an equal underground reserve, registered map node and hidden data-only reserve actor. Blocked clicks keep the preview active so you can move and try again. The click is rechecked immediately before allocation. Preview-only clicks report the plan and never allocate a reserve, clump or node.",["examples"]={"mobs.spawn_deposit iron 1000 preview","mobs.spawn_deposit iron 1000","mobs.spawn_deposit clay 2000 rich preview","mobs.spawn_deposit clay 2000 rich","mobs.spawn_deposit salt 1500","mobs.cancel"},["notes"]="The screenshot error Mineral resource template or native size unavailable came from reading generic ResourceTemplate fields that are NULL for minerals on 0.8.117; the native engine owns separate Iron/Clay/Salt classes. This release uses those classes and native scale instead. 1000 means 1000 surface units plus 1000 underground units. Rich reserves follow native deep-mining rules and may display as endless. The ring indicates mining range, not a strict empty clearance circle. The centre must be on valid owned terrain and outside native blockers; centres within 1m of an existing underground deposit are refused to prevent accidental duplicates. This does not guarantee mine access on cliffs or awkward terrain. No random map-generator relocation or new custom game assets. Placement has no undo; partial native failure stops the tool. Remove underground and surface layers separately when cleaning up. User testing confirmed placement and mineral-imprint cleanup. Extended mining and save/reload checks remain open; offline checks are not gameplay proof. The placed iron/clay/salt deposit has no terrain artwork or extra ore model, matching natural deposits; only its map icon/tooltip remain. The ground material, radius and crosshair are temporary placement guides. Earlier Mobs paper-map imprints are hidden automatically after load or by refresh_resource_icons, without deleting reserves. Surface stones remain visible.",["related"]={"remove_deposit","resource","deposit","cancel"}},["mobs.remove_deposit"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing.",["steps"]="Choose iron, clay, salt or all, close the console and click near the underground reserve. Preview first.",["examples"]={"mobs.remove_deposit iron preview","mobs.remove_deposit iron","mobs.resource remove iron preview"},["notes"]="Removes underground reserves/decal and colocated empty legacy markers. Real surface clumps remain deliberately: remove them separately using resource remove. all means nearest matching kind, not every deposit on the map. No undo.",["related"]={"resource","deposit"}},["mobs.deposit"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing.",["steps"]="Use add to increase an EXISTING underground reserve, or rich/normal to change its flag. Click within 2500 of the reserve.",["examples"]={"mobs.deposit add iron 1000 preview","mobs.deposit add iron 1000","mobs.deposit rich iron"},["notes"]="Cannot edit a surface-only resource group. A visible icon alone does not prove an underground reserve exists. Use resource add for surface ore; spawn_deposit creates both layers in new versions.",["related"]={"undo_deposit","resource","spawn_deposit"}},["mobs.undo_deposit"]={["target"]="Latest unchanged underground reserve edit in this session.",["steps"]="Undo an add/rich/normal edit after confirming no extraction or later edit changed the target.",["examples"]={"mobs.deposit add iron 100","mobs.undo_deposit"},["notes"]="Ten edits retained until player/mod reload. Does not undo creation/removal or rebuild a deleted deposit.",["related"]={"deposit","remove_deposit"}},["mobs.pond"]={["target"]="place opens a moving pond-footprint preview on owned terrain. Close the console, move the cursor and read green READY or red BLOCKED. Left-click confirms only a valid site; right-click or mobs.cancel cancels. The tool expires after five minutes. Relaxed placement is the default; add strict only to restore the old restrictive rules. remove uses a separate one-shot click.",["steps"]="Run mobs.pond place for relaxed placement: check the actual pond polygon, without a surrounding clearance rectangle or extra margin. Allow up to 10 metres of height variation across the footprint and crossing into neighbouring regions owned by the same lord. Valid terrain and native navigation/building blocker checks still apply. Left-click a READY site to create one completed empty pond, then stock it with pond_fish. Blocked clicks keep the tool active. mobs.pond place strict restores the full rectangle plus 1 metre, a 2-metre height limit and a single-region requirement. Add preview to either mode for repeated read-only checks; no pond is created.",["examples"]={"mobs.pond place","mobs.pond place preview","mobs.pond place strict preview","mobs.pond_fish 500","mobs.pond remove preview"},["notes"]="The pond size is unchanged; relaxed placement stops rejecting unused corners of its bounding rectangle. Its ghost shows only the actual outline, while strict also shows the old outer clearance rectangle. The coloured READY/BLOCKED label includes specific reasons for terrain, ownership or native blockers. The outline is a footprint guide, not the final water/terrain deformation. More uneven terrain may produce rougher banks; the 10-metre limit is a placement policy, not a proven guarantee of attractive or usable shores. Both preview and apply use the same native plan and recheck the exact click. Existing unfinished ponds are not reinitialized; stock fish separately. User testing confirmed improved pond placement. Actual catches and extended persistence checks remain open.",["related"]={"pond_fish","finish_constructions"}},["mobs.pond_fish"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing.",["steps"]="Run the command, close the console and click near a completed owned Fishing Pond (within 1500 game units). New mobs.pond place ponds are already complete. Fish use a native pond placement transform rather than the building origin.",["examples"]={"mobs.pond_fish 500 preview","mobs.pond_fish 500","mobs.refill_resources fish preview"},["notes"]="Adds one shoal to the nearest completed owned Fishing Pond. Existing shoals are rejected to prevent duplicates; refill existing fish instead. Worker harvesting and save/load need live confirmation. No undo. 0.16.1 checks the native constructed state again at apply and uses the pond's generated fish anchor; missing anchors produce an explicit refusal.",["related"]={"pond","resources","refill_resources"}},["mobs.grow_trees"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Preview the eligible world-tree records, run normally, and wait for the completion notification. Work runs in bounded batches.",["examples"]={"mobs.grow_trees preview","mobs.grow_trees"},["notes"]="Grows native young and intermediate world-tree stages to maturity, including previously untracked stages; decorative bushes are excluded. Blocked transitions are reported rather than counted as successful. Does not plant an entire new forest. No undo.",["related"]={"grow_saplings","grow_stage","replant_trees"}},["mobs.grow_saplings"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin. For area, select ONE owned building with an explicitly limited work area.",["steps"]="Preview first. grow_saplings matures registered plantings, including forester saplings. grow_stage advances each eligible record one native stage instead of fully maturing it.",["examples"]={"mobs.grow_saplings preview","mobs.grow_saplings","mobs.grow_saplings area preview"},["notes"]="The area scope uses the selected building work circle, not the camera viewport. Native transitions can be blocked. Completion may run in batches; cancel stops future batches only. No undo.",["related"]={"grow_trees","plants","cancel"}},["mobs.grow_stage"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin. For area, select ONE owned building with an explicitly limited work area.",["steps"]="Preview first. grow_saplings matures registered plantings, including forester saplings. grow_stage advances each eligible record one native stage instead of fully maturing it.",["examples"]={"mobs.grow_stage area preview"},["notes"]="The area scope uses the selected building work circle, not the camera viewport. Native transitions can be blocked. Completion may run in batches; cancel stops future batches only. No undo.",["related"]={"grow_trees","plants","cancel"}},["mobs.replant_trees"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing. The command-target region must also match the intended owned ground.",["steps"]="replant_trees places ONE oak sapling on cleared ground. regrow_trees combines that single replant click with maturation of eligible native trees in the target region.",["examples"]={"mobs.replant_trees preview","mobs.replant_trees"},["notes"]="This is one sapling per click, not a forest brush. Native collision checks still apply. Existing saplings and world trees can instead be matured without planting by grow_saplings/grow_trees. No undo.",["related"]={"grow_trees","grow_saplings"}},["mobs.regrow_trees"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing. The command-target region must also match the intended owned ground.",["steps"]="replant_trees places ONE oak sapling on cleared ground. regrow_trees combines that single replant click with maturation of eligible native trees in the target region.",["examples"]={"mobs.regrow_trees preview"},["notes"]="This is one sapling per click, not a forest brush. Native collision checks still apply. Existing saplings and world trees can instead be matured without planting by grow_saplings/grow_trees. No undo.",["related"]={"grow_trees","grow_saplings"}},["mobs.fertility"]={["target"]="Select the owned building in the normal game view BEFORE opening the console. A pinned region does not select buildings. Up to 32 buildings only where the command explicitly allows a batch. fertilization region explicitly uses the owned command-target region instead.",["steps"]="fertility reads existing crop fertility and fertilization counters. fertilization toggles permission, with selected/region scope and optional preview.",["examples"]={"mobs.fertility wheat"},["notes"]="Permission does not add soil fertility or bypass game prerequisites. Use soil for actual grid edits. Rye and oats are included in fertility inspection.",["related"]={"soil","undo_fertilization","plants"}},["mobs.fertilization"]={["target"]="Select the owned building in the normal game view BEFORE opening the console. A pinned region does not select buildings. Up to 32 buildings only where the command explicitly allows a batch. fertilization region explicitly uses the owned command-target region instead.",["steps"]="fertility reads existing crop fertility and fertilization counters. fertilization toggles permission, with selected/region scope and optional preview.",["examples"]={"mobs.fertilization on selected preview","mobs.fertilization on region"},["notes"]="Permission does not add soil fertility or bypass game prerequisites. Use soil for actual grid edits. Rye and oats are included in fertility inspection.",["related"]={"soil","undo_fertilization","plants"}},["mobs.undo_fertilization"]={["target"]="Latest unchanged fertilization-permission batch.",["steps"]="Run after a permission toggle to restore previous permissions.",["examples"]={"mobs.fertilization on selected","mobs.undo_fertilization"},["notes"]="Five batches retained until reload. Changed ownership or permission values cause refusal. This does not restore soil fertility.",["related"]={"fertilization","soil"}},["mobs.soil"]={["target"]="Select the owned building in the normal game view BEFORE opening the console. A pinned region does not select buildings. Up to 32 buildings only where the command explicitly allows a batch.",["steps"]="For selected scope, select planted fields/plots. For area, set an explicit limited work area on each selected owned building. set takes a percentage; restore has no percentage argument. Preview first.",["examples"]={"mobs.soil set all 100 selected preview","mobs.soil set wheat 80 selected","mobs.soil restore all selected preview","mobs.soil restore barley area preview"},["notes"]="set changes baseline AND current fertility. restore removes depletion up to existing baseline, so it does not make poor baseline soil perfect. Rye shares wheat soil; oats share barley. Unplanted plots can select zero cells: use plants to inspect or a limited work area. Overlay may refresh later.",["related"]={"plants","fertility","undo_soil"}},["mobs.plants"]={["target"]="Select the owned building in the normal game view BEFORE opening the console. A pinned region does not select buildings. Up to 32 buildings only where the command explicitly allows a batch.",["steps"]="Select planted fields or a forestry building, then inspect plant records.",["examples"]={"mobs.plants"},["notes"]="Read-only: prints counts and up to 100 records with type, position, growth, yield and soil-cell index. It does not plant, harvest or change fertility.",["related"]={"soil","grow_saplings"}},["mobs.undo_soil"]={["target"]="Latest unchanged soil batch in the same loaded settlement.",["steps"]="Preview the restoration, then run without preview.",["examples"]={"mobs.undo_soil preview","mobs.undo_soil"},["notes"]="Refuses if edited values or ownership changed, rather than overwriting newer simulation changes. Only the latest native soil batch is retained.",["related"]={"soil","fertility"}},["mobs.perks"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Open Development once to load the card table, then list/search cards. Use the displayed number or a unique key with add/remove; clear removes extras.",["examples"]={"mobs.perks list","mobs.perks add BambergSmallholders preview","mobs.perks add BambergSmallholders"},["notes"]="Cards are regional Origins/Rural Foundations, not development-tree points. Extras include penalties; shared effects apply once. The vanilla screen shows primary cards only. Numbers refer to this listing, not item IDs.",["related"]={"perk_add","perk_remove","respec_perks"}},["mobs.perk_add"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="List cards, then add a listed number or unique key. Preview first. mobs.perks add is the friendlier equivalent.",["examples"]={"mobs.perks list","mobs.perk_add BambergSmallholders preview","mobs.perks add BambergSmallholders"},["notes"]="Keeps primary cards and applies an extra regional card including its penalties. Primary cards cannot be added twice. Preserve Native/State when upgrading. Full save/load behavior needs continued confirmation.",["related"]={"perk_remove","perk_clear","perks"}},["mobs.perks_add"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="List cards, then add a listed number or unique key. Preview first. mobs.perks add is the friendlier equivalent.",["examples"]={"mobs.perks_add BambergSmallholders preview"},["notes"]="Keeps primary cards and applies an extra regional card including its penalties. Primary cards cannot be added twice. Preserve Native/State when upgrading. Full save/load behavior needs continued confirmation.",["related"]={"perk_remove","perk_clear","perks"}},["mobs.perk_remove"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Remove an extra card by its listed number or unique key. Preview checks the plan before rebuilding effects.",["examples"]={"mobs.perk_remove BambergSmallholders preview","mobs.perks remove BambergSmallholders"},["notes"]="Preserves primary cards and effects supplied by other active cards. This is the companion reversal for an added extra; respec handles primary choices.",["related"]={"perk_add","perk_clear","respec_perks"}},["mobs.perks_remove"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Remove an extra card by its listed number or unique key. Preview checks the plan before rebuilding effects.",["examples"]={"mobs.perks_remove BambergSmallholders preview"},["notes"]="Preserves primary cards and effects supplied by other active cards. This is the companion reversal for an added extra; respec handles primary choices.",["related"]={"perk_add","perk_clear","respec_perks"}},["mobs.perk_clear"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Preview, then clear extra regional cards while keeping normal primary choices.",["examples"]={"mobs.perk_clear preview","mobs.perks clear"},["notes"]="Includes all extras in this region only. Effects are rebuilt from the retained primaries; perks_clear is an alias.",["related"]={"perk_remove","respec_perks"}},["mobs.perks_clear"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Preview, then clear extra regional cards while keeping normal primary choices.",["examples"]={"mobs.perks_clear preview"},["notes"]="Includes all extras in this region only. Effects are rebuilt from the retained primaries; perks_clear is an alias.",["related"]={"perk_remove","respec_perks"}},["mobs.perk_points"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="perk_points restores a tier choice by resetting that tier. respec_perks clears the specified primary choice(s) and rebuilds effects; default is both. Preview first.",["examples"]={"mobs.perk_points 2 preview","mobs.perk_points both"},["notes"]="Not a numeric currency editor and not development-tree points. Resetting tier 1 ALSO resets tier 2 because of the dependency. Settlement unlock gates remain.",["related"]={"perks","perk_add"}},["mobs.respec_perks"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="perk_points restores a tier choice by resetting that tier. respec_perks clears the specified primary choice(s) and rebuilds effects; default is both. Preview first.",["examples"]={"mobs.respec_perks all preview"},["notes"]="Not a numeric currency editor and not development-tree points. Resetting tier 1 ALSO resets tier 2 because of the dependency. Settlement unlock gates remain.",["related"]={"perks","perk_add"}},["mobs.grow_population"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Run status to inspect approval, the game natural monthly growth result, usable housing places and homeless families. Preview the requested 1..10 PEOPLE, then run without preview to create them now through the native resident/family/home path. Existing incomplete eligible families are filled first; new families use vacant completed housing. No click is needed.",["examples"]={"mobs.grow_population status","mobs.grow_population 3 preview","mobs.grow_population 3","mobs.grow_population 10 preview"},["notes"]="0.16.0-alpha.3 changes the number from repeated growth attempts to actual people, not families. Default 1; maximum 10 per call. Explicit creation bypasses the natural approval/arrival-day gates without changing the date or forcing approval. All planned home entrances are preflighted before creation; enough housing is required for the whole request. Sleeping/unfinished/mourning homes are excluded. Existing homeless families take priority over new households. Native failures stop and report actual population change without retrying or rolling back earlier arrivals. New population has ordinary needs and can later leave under normal game rules. Live/save-load confirmation remains pending. No undo.",["related"]={"approval","rehouse","regions","status"}},["mobs.skip_mourning"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Preview buildings with active mourning timers, then run normally to clear them.",["examples"]={"mobs.skip_mourning preview","mobs.skip_mourning"},["notes"]="This clears timers in the target region. It does not revive deceased residents or add a family. No undo.",["related"]={"grow_population","approval"}},["mobs.livestock_cooldown"]={["target"]="Your owned command-target region. Run mobs.regions, then mobs.region with a listed ID; confirm mobs.status. mobs.region auto clears the pin.",["steps"]="Run without arguments to inspect the next livestock-order cooldown; reset clears that cooldown.",["examples"]={"mobs.livestock_cooldown","mobs.livestock_cooldown reset"},["notes"]="Does not order, spawn or deliver animals, and does not fill a trading post inventory.",["related"]={"animal"}},["mobs.animal"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing.",["steps"]="Choose ox, horse, mule, sheep, lamb, goat, pig, chicken, hound, cow, calf, deer or hare; optionally 1..20 animals and preview.",["examples"]={"mobs.animal ox 1 preview","mobs.animal sheep 3"},["notes"]="These are individual native spawned animals. deer/hare here do NOT create a registered hunting resource node; a hunting icon/working herd is not implemented. Do not use item IDs. No undo.",["related"]={"livestock_cooldown","spawn_resource","spawn_wildlife"}},["mobs.unit"]={["target"]="Hover the intended living owned unit; follow it before opening the console if hover is lost. rehouse also needs one selected owned completed house.",["steps"]="unit inspects; rename_unit accepts a multiword name; undo_unit_name restores a guarded rename. follow tracks the camera; off stops it. rehouse selected moves the hovered/followed family after capacity checks.",["examples"]={"mobs.unit"},["notes"]="Renaming requires an owned home. Rehousing stays in the same region and checks housing capacity; no undo for family moves. Follow can normalize game speed. A region pin does not select a unit.",["related"]={"teleport","building"}},["mobs.rename_unit"]={["target"]="Hover the intended living owned unit; follow it before opening the console if hover is lost. rehouse also needs one selected owned completed house.",["steps"]="unit inspects; rename_unit accepts a multiword name; undo_unit_name restores a guarded rename. follow tracks the camera; off stops it. rehouse selected moves the hovered/followed family after capacity checks.",["examples"]={"mobs.rename_unit New Name"},["notes"]="Renaming requires an owned home. Rehousing stays in the same region and checks housing capacity; no undo for family moves. Follow can normalize game speed. A region pin does not select a unit.",["related"]={"teleport","building"}},["mobs.undo_unit_name"]={["target"]="Hover the intended living owned unit; follow it before opening the console if hover is lost. rehouse also needs one selected owned completed house.",["steps"]="unit inspects; rename_unit accepts a multiword name; undo_unit_name restores a guarded rename. follow tracks the camera; off stops it. rehouse selected moves the hovered/followed family after capacity checks.",["examples"]={"mobs.undo_unit_name"},["notes"]="Renaming requires an owned home. Rehousing stays in the same region and checks housing capacity; no undo for family moves. Follow can normalize game speed. A region pin does not select a unit.",["related"]={"teleport","building"}},["mobs.follow"]={["target"]="Hover the intended living owned unit; follow it before opening the console if hover is lost. rehouse also needs one selected owned completed house.",["steps"]="unit inspects; rename_unit accepts a multiword name; undo_unit_name restores a guarded rename. follow tracks the camera; off stops it. rehouse selected moves the hovered/followed family after capacity checks.",["examples"]={"mobs.follow","mobs.follow off"},["notes"]="Renaming requires an owned home. Rehousing stays in the same region and checks housing capacity; no undo for family moves. Follow can normalize game speed. A region pin does not select a unit.",["related"]={"teleport","building"}},["mobs.rehouse"]={["target"]="Hover the intended living owned unit; follow it before opening the console if hover is lost. rehouse also needs one selected owned completed house.",["steps"]="unit inspects; rename_unit accepts a multiword name; undo_unit_name restores a guarded rename. follow tracks the camera; off stops it. rehouse selected moves the hovered/followed family after capacity checks.",["examples"]={"mobs.rehouse selected preview"},["notes"]="Renaming requires an owned home. Rehousing stays in the same region and checks housing capacity; no undo for family moves. Follow can normalize game speed. A region pin does not select a unit.",["related"]={"teleport","building"}},["mobs.teleport"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing. unit uses your hovered/followed owned unit; squads uses selected owned squads.",["steps"]="Select/follow the targets first, run unit or squads with preview, then close the console and click the destination.",["examples"]={"mobs.teleport unit preview","mobs.teleport squads preview"},["notes"]="Formation offsets are preserved for squads. Existing orders remain active, so units may move again immediately. No undo.",["related"]={"unit","follow"}},["mobs.claim"]={["target"]="Explicit map selection or a real region ID from mobs.map_regions.",["steps"]="Start a claim without influence cost, or finish a claim already belonging to your lord. Preview before applying; all is supported for existing claims when appropriate.",["examples"]={"mobs.claim start preview","mobs.claim finish all preview"},["notes"]="Not the same as choosing the command-target region. Finish requires a valid existing claim; it does not simply grant arbitrary foreign land. No undo.",["related"]={"map_regions","region"}},["mobs.mercenaries"]={["target"]="Your player lord.",["steps"]="Use the literal reroll subcommand, then reopen the hiring panel.",["examples"]={"mobs.mercenaries reroll"},["notes"]="Changes offers through the game; does not hire or pay units. No undo.",["related"]={"bandits","raiders"}},["mobs.bandits"]={["target"]="Map-wide native bandit-camp placement rules.",["steps"]="Preview, then request a camp at a valid random game-chosen location.",["examples"]={"mobs.bandits preview","mobs.bandits"},["notes"]="This asks the game to choose a valid site; it does not place a camp at your mouse click. No undo.",["related"]={"bandit_camp","raiders"}},["mobs.bandit_camp"]={["target"]="Clear UNCLAIMED ground, away from building borders.",["steps"]="Run with preview, close the console and click clear unclaimed ground. Repeat without preview to request a real camp squad/order, then resume simulation.",["examples"]={"mobs.bandit_camp preview","mobs.bandit_camp"},["notes"]="Owned or foreign-claimed ground is rejected. This is hostile content, not your own settlement troops. No undo.",["related"]={"bandits","raiders"}},["mobs.raiders"]={["target"]="A playable clicked region; this tool can create hostile squads.",["steps"]="Choose 1..6 squads, preview, close the console and click the region.",["examples"]={"mobs.raiders 1 preview"},["notes"]="Creates hostile raiders rather than recruiting your militia. No undo.",["related"]={"bandits","mercenaries"}},["mobs.weather"]={["target"]="Whole map weather simulation.",["steps"]="Choose rain, drought, clear, end_rain or end_drought. instant requests immediate transition; damaging applies only to rain. Preview first.",["examples"]={"mobs.weather rain preview","mobs.weather clear instant","mobs.weather drought instant preview"},["notes"]="The simulation can later choose new weather. clear ends rain and drought; end_rain/end_drought affect the chosen condition. No undo.",["related"]={"speed","skip_day"}},["mobs.speed"]={["target"]="Global game simulation.",["steps"]="Run without arguments to read speed, or choose 0..12. Zero pauses and one resumes normally.",["examples"]={"mobs.speed","mobs.speed 0","mobs.speed 1"},["notes"]="Uses the native speed request. High speed may alter performance and make changes harder to observe. This does not advance an exact number of days.",["related"]={"skip_day","construction"}},["mobs.skip_day"]={["target"]="Global game calendar.",["steps"]="Preview a count from 1..30, then request native day updates if intended.",["examples"]={"mobs.skip_day 1 preview","mobs.skip_day 1"},["notes"]="Daily simulation events may run. It is not a guarantee that workers finish travel/jobs or that population appears. No undo.",["related"]={"speed","grow_population"}},["mobs.boop"]={["target"]="Player native debug mode.",["steps"]="Read status or explicitly turn the setting on/off. With no argument the current mode toggles.",["examples"]={"mobs.boop status","mobs.boop on","mobs.boop off"},["notes"]="This exposes the native debug Boop setting, not a documented task-assignment API. Use only when you want that native mode; not required for normal commands.",["related"]={"debug_task"}},["mobs.foreign_supply"]={["target"]="Loaded global foreign-market supply.",["steps"]="Read all entries or filter by display name/item ID.",["examples"]={"mobs.foreign_supply","mobs.foreign_supply iron"},["notes"]="Read-only global market information; not stock in your target region and not a delivery.",["related"]={"stock","inventory"}},["mobs.run"]={["target"]="Local text files inside this mod Commands folder.",["steps"]="Write one exact Mobs command per line in a .txt file. Preview displays the commands; remove preview to run them in order.",["examples"]={"mobs.run example.txt preview"},["notes"]="Only up to 100 lines/64 KiB. No scripts, path traversal or recursive run. Stops at first error; prior successful mutations remain. Do not put several click placements in one file: each arms a pending tool rather than completing a click.",["related"]={"recent","cancel"}},["help"]={["target"]="Read-only discovery; no settlement required unless loaded game data is being requested.",["steps"]="Open the console and browse the dashboard or searchable help. Copy exact command syntax; replace placeholders and omit brackets.",["examples"]={"mobs","mobs.help construction","help region"},["notes"]="help is an alias for mobs.help. mobs uses exact command matching when dispatching actions; typo matches only suggest.",["related"]={"find","advice","tutorial"}},["mobs.spawn_wildlife"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing.",["steps"]="Choose deer or hare, optionally rich, and preview first. Close the console and click clear ground in an owned region. The resource node and herd home are placed at that click; animals are distributed nearby. All planned animal sites are checked for valid native height, the same region and native blockers before any squad or animal is created. Repeat without preview and click the same spot to apply. Include the site in a staffed hunting camp work area and resume simulation.",["examples"]={"mobs.spawn_wildlife deer preview","mobs.spawn_wildlife deer","mobs.spawn_wildlife deer rich","mobs.spawn_wildlife hare"},["notes"]="0.16 alpha; actual hunting and save/reload await user testing. Population is the midpoint of the game normal/rich population range (bounded to 1..256), so preview and apply agree. Animals begin within 1000 game units of the clicked node and can wander under normal game AI. Blocked or border-crossing placements are refused before spawning. One herd per applied click. Existing mobs.animal deer/hare remains individual spawning. No undo; do not repeat placement if registration reports an incomplete result.",["related"]={"animal","resources","refresh_resource_icons","cancel"}},["mobs.repair_fishing"]={["target"]="Run the command, close the console, then click the intended location in an owned region. It is a one-shot tool with a five-minute expiry. mobs.cancel disarms it. Preview also requires the click, but changes nothing.",["steps"]="Default kind is eel. Run preview, close the console and click near the actual shoal, within 2500 game units. Read the planned identity, regional registration and availability-tag counts. Repeat without preview and click the SAME shoal. Resume simulation; ensure a staffed fishing workplace has access to appropriate water. Check actual catches, then save separately and reload.",["examples"]={"mobs.repair_fishing preview","mobs.repair_fishing eel","mobs.repair_fishing fish preview","mobs.repair_fishing fish"},["notes"]="Candidate repair for existing eel/fish nodes; worker harvesting and persistence are not yet verified. Restores the live game template identity/seasonal flag, native placement height, region resource registration, availability tag and map view/HUD. Amounts, capacity and richness remain unchanged. Rejects unavailable template defaults, other resource kinds and building-attached pond fish. Fish and eel never substitute for each other. Does not create a missing/deleted shoal, fix every shoreline/reachability problem, or undo earlier depletion. No undo.",["related"]={"spawn_resource","resource","pond_fish","refresh_resource_icons"}}},["tutorial"]={{["key"]="start",["title"]="Install, check versions and read command syntax",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.version","mobs.advice.help","mobs.advice.advice"},["paragraphs"]={"This alpha targets Manor Lords 0.8.117 with a compatible UE4SS loader and ConsoleEnablerMod. The original MLConsoleCommands mod is not required. Install the MLConsoleCommandsByMobs folder under ManorLords/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods, with enabled.txt present. Restart to load changed native helpers. Keep Native/State and custom Commands files when upgrading.","Load a settlement and open your configured console key (F10 in the development setup). Run mobs.version, mobs.ping and mobs. A responding handler proves loading, not that every game action works. Use mobs.help to browse and mobs.find <words> to search.","Angle brackets mean required input; square brackets mean optional input. Pipes separate alternatives. Replace placeholders, omit brackets, and type only one choice. Example: mobs.treasury add 1000. Do not type mobs.treasury <set|add> <amount>.","mobs.advice.pile explains a command without running it. mobs.advice pile is equivalent. mobs.tutorial all prints this entire manual; mobs.tutorial resources opens one chapter. Each guide also links to its wiki page."}},{["key"]="targeting",["title"]="Choose a region, select buildings and use click tools",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.regions","mobs.advice.region","mobs.advice.status","mobs.advice.cancel"},["paragraphs"]={"Region commands resolve the pinned target, otherwise selected map region, otherwise current region. Run mobs.regions to list OWNED IDs, mobs.region with an actual listed ID to pin one, then mobs.status to confirm. mobs.region current pins the current region; mobs.region auto clears the pin. IDs are save-specific.","Building commands use actual selection: close the console, click the owned building/field until its information panel is visible, then reopen the console. mobs.building and mobs.inventory inspect a single selected building. A region pin does not select a building. Multi-building actions validate every target before the first write.","Click commands first ARM a tool. Close the console, then click/place the target. They expire after five minutes; mobs.cancel stops pending tools. A preview also needs the click to resolve the target but changes nothing. After a successful preview, enter the real command and click again.","Ownership checks are deliberate. Resources normally require owned ground; bandit_camp instead requires unclaimed ground. A message saying armed does not mean anything was delivered or created yet. Read the later result message."}},{["key"]="discovery",["title"]="Autocomplete, search, advice and recent commands",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.autocomplete","mobs.advice.complete","mobs.advice.find","mobs.advice.recent"},["paragraphs"]={"Type mobs. for command names; Tab completes text and Enter executes it. Item variants appear only after a complete item-taking command, so the broad dropdown is not filled by thousands of IDs. Type mobs.pile to reach its item choices.","mobs.autocomplete refresh reloads item/region/card suggestions. Open Development once if card data is not loaded. mobs.autocomplete off disables native suggestions for this session. If native suggestions fail, mobs.complete pile br prints contextual choices and mobs.find supplies ranked typo-tolerant search.","Unknown/ambiguous input is never silently corrected into a gameplay action. Use mobs.advice.<short command> for the target, exact workflow, examples, limits and related commands. mobs.recent 30 prints successful command strings without replaying them. It clears on reload.","Runtime item names may be localized and may differ from internal enum labels. Use mobs.items <search> and copy its numeric ID when a name is ambiguous. Read the wiki item table to discover IDs; verify deliverability in mobs.items."}},{["key"]="supplies",["title"]="Items, new piles, clicked deliveries and inventories",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.items","mobs.advice.pile","mobs.advice.drop","mobs.advice.give","mobs.advice.inventory_add"},["paragraphs"]={"Find items: mobs.items bread, mobs.items planks, or mobs.items 17. mobs.pile 17 100 starts native Supplies placement for 100 planks. Close the console and place the preview on owned ground. This makes a new pile and fills it once, after successful placement.","mobs.drop 17 20 arms delivery to clicked owned storage, a pile or a site needing planks. It does not create piles on bare ground. Ineligible clicks leave it armed. mobs.drop with no arguments reads pending status; mobs.cancel cancels.","For already selected buildings, mobs.give 17 20 preview calculates a batch without changing inventory; mobs.give 17 20 applies it. The amount is EACH building, not a shared budget. Production/housing inventories instead use mobs.inventory_add, which can bypass completed-building storage caps.","Construction accepts only its missing materials, accounting for goods already stored and incoming. No generic delivery undo exists. Inspect local goods with mobs.inventory and regional totals with mobs.stock; they are different scopes.","To clean clutter, mobs.clear_empty_piles preview lists confirmed-empty piles in the target region. Run without preview to remove them. mobs.remove_selected_piles preview checks selected Supplies piles; the real command deletes those piles INCLUDING CONTENTS. There is no undo for removal."}},{["key"]="construction",["title"]="Supply sites, finish work and control new builds",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.construction_needs","mobs.advice.supply_construction","mobs.advice.finish_constructions","mobs.advice.instant_build"},["paragraphs"]={"Set the region and check mobs.status. mobs.construction_needs region reports missing material totals. Select one site and run mobs.construction_needs for its detailed bill, including incoming deliveries.","mobs.supply_construction preview supplies a plan for the target region; selected limits the scope to selected owned unfinished/upgrading buildings. Removing preview supplies materials only, not work.","mobs.finish_constructions preview counts unfinished sites. mobs.finish_constructions prepares materials/work through the game. Resume with mobs.speed 1 and let the simulation finalize the sites. Workers can still need to reach them; read per-site failures instead of repeatedly assuming completion.","mobs.construction pause/resume controls unfinished sites in the target region. mobs.instant_build on affects newly placed buildings globally for the session, including materials; switch it off after intended placement. Existing sites use finish_constructions. Demolition uses mobs.demolish selected preview, then the real command with native refund rules and no undo."}},{["key"]="resources",["title"]="Create berries/minerals, understand layers and remove nodes",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.spawn_resource","mobs.advice.resource","mobs.advice.spawn_deposit New mineral placement uses a moving native-material preview, centre crosshair and mining-radius ring. Close the console, move to READY owned ground and left-click the exact centre. Blocked clicks stay armed; right-click cancels. Add preview to inspect repeatedly without creating either layer.","mobs.advice.deposit","mobs.advice.remove_deposit","mobs.advice.refresh_resource_icons","mobs.advice.spawn_wildlife","mobs.advice.repair_fishing"},["paragraphs"]={"Berries example: mobs.spawn_resource berries 100 4 preview; close console and click owned ground. This previews FOUR clumps of 100 each, not 100 spread across the group. Repeat without preview and click to create it. Optional rich comes after amount/count: mobs.spawn_resource iron 1000 1 rich.","Kinds are iron, clay, salt, stone, berries, mushrooms, fish and eel. Deer/hares are not supported hunting-node kinds. mobs.resources berries inspects existing clumps in the target region; mobs.refill_resources berries preview refills them to capacity rather than creating new ones.","There are TWO mineral layers: visible finite surface clumps and underground reserves for deep extraction. mobs.resource add iron 100 edits one existing surface clump. mobs.deposit add iron 100 edits an existing underground reserve. A surface icon alone does not prove an underground reserve exists.","New mobs.spawn_deposit iron 1000 rich creates 1000 surface units PLUS 1000 underground units and a ground-facing decal. Rich deep reserves follow native endless/deep-mining rules. The finite amount shown in the resource tooltip comes from the surface clump. Legacy 0.14.0 placements could have only an empty marker, with no finite surface amount. New mineral placement uses a moving native-material preview, centre crosshair and mining-radius ring. Close the console, move to READY owned ground and left-click the exact centre. Blocked clicks stay armed; right-click cancels. Add preview to inspect repeatedly without creating either layer.","To remove surface fish: mobs.resource remove fish preview, close console and click close to the shoal. For eel use eel explicitly; fish never silently selects eel. Remove deletes the whole group; remove_clump deletes one clump. Matching distance is 2500 game units, and ownership still applies.","mobs.remove_deposit iron preview removes underground reserves/decal and colocated EMPTY legacy markers. Real surface clumps stay until mobs.resource remove iron. If an old stripe was already removed but its empty marker remains, mobs.resource remove iron can now remove that marker. Preview first; removals have no undo.","For visible models but missing normal-map icons or paper-map hover details, run mobs.refresh_resource_icons. For older badly scaled land clumps, mobs.resource refresh berries preview repairs size/height/view after a click without changing goods. Do not spawn duplicate nodes to fix an icon.","Spawned fish/eel still need suitable water, worker reachability and native seasonal conditions. The reported eel harvesting/despawn issue remains unconfirmed; do not treat an icon and a full counter as proof that workers can harvest it.","The 0.16 alpha adds mobs.repair_fishing eel preview for an existing shoal: click nearby, inspect the plan, repeat without preview, then check catches and save/reload. It restores native aquatic identity, seasonal behavior and regional availability without refilling goods. Fish use the explicit fish argument. Actual catches and persistence still need gameplay confirmation."}},{["key"]="fishing",["title"]="Fishing Ponds, natural fish and eel",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.pond","mobs.advice.pond_fish","mobs.advice.refill_resources","mobs.advice.resource"},["paragraphs"]={"mobs.pond place opens a moving footprint preview with relaxed rules: the actual pond outline, no extra margin, up to 10 metres of height variation and neighbouring regions owned by your lord. Close the console and read green READY or red BLOCKED with the reason. Left-click a valid site for one completed empty pond; blocked clicks keep the tool active. Right-click or mobs.cancel cancels. mobs.pond place preview stays read-only. Add strict to restore the old rectangle, 1-metre margin, 2-metre height limit and single-region rule. No builders are needed; stock fish separately. Existing unfinished ponds are not reinitialized.","Run mobs.pond_fish 500 preview, close the console and click within 1500 game units of the completed owned pond. Repeat without preview to add ONE shoal. Existing fish are rejected rather than duplicated; use mobs.refill_resources fish preview for an existing shoal.","Natural-water groups use mobs.spawn_resource fish or mobs.spawn_resource eel with suitable placement. This differs from putting fish food in a granary or creating a pond building. Fish and eel are different resource kinds; inspect mobs.resources to choose correctly.","If workers ignore a new shoal, record the exact command, month/season, fishing building type, work area, water placement and behavior after reload. Worker usability and save/load of spawned shoals still require live confirmation. Removal of a pond and removal of its resource are separate operations; preview before deleting anything."}},{["key"]="forestry",["title"]="World trees, intermediate stages and forester plantings",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.grow_trees","mobs.advice.grow_saplings","mobs.advice.grow_stage","mobs.advice.replant_trees","mobs.advice.regrow_trees"},["paragraphs"]={"mobs.grow_trees preview finds eligible world-tree growth records, including untracked young/intermediate stages. mobs.grow_trees processes them in batches until native maturity or a reported blocked state. Wait for the completion message.","mobs.grow_saplings targets registered saplings, including those planted by foresters. mobs.grow_stage advances each eligible record once instead of forcing maturity. Add area to limit either tool to ONE selected owned building with an explicit limited work circle.","mobs.replant_trees arms one oak-sapling replant click on cleared owned ground. It is one tree per placement, not a brush that fills a region. mobs.regrow_trees combines the one-tree replant click with region growth.","Decorative bushes are not trees for these tools. Native collision checks and growth transitions can refuse records. mobs.cancel stops future clicks/batches; it does not reverse growth already performed. There is no forestry undo."}},{["key"]="farming",["title"]="Read fertility, edit soil and inspect planted crops",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.fertility","mobs.advice.fertilization","mobs.advice.soil","mobs.advice.plants","mobs.advice.undo_soil"},["paragraphs"]={"Select an owned field before opening the console. mobs.fertility wheat reads native averages and fertilization counters. mobs.fertilization on selected preview toggles fertilization PERMISSION; it does not restore exhausted soil and does not bypass fertilization prerequisites.","mobs.soil set all 100 selected preview plans actual soil-grid changes for planted cells. Without preview it sets current and baseline fertility. mobs.soil restore all selected instead restores depletion up to the current baseline; a naturally poor baseline remains poor.","For area scope, select an owned building and first define an explicit limited work circle. mobs.soil restore barley area preview targets cells in that work area. Area does not mean the camera view or all fields in the pinned region.","Only wheat, flax and barley channels exist here. Rye shares wheat; oats share barley. Unplanted fields can select zero planted cells, so inspect mobs.plants or use a limited work area. Fertility overlays may update later than stored values.","mobs.undo_soil preview checks the latest batch and refuses newer changed values or changed ownership. mobs.undo_fertilization is a separate permission undo. Neither is a general save rollback."}},{["key"]="perks",["title"]="Regional cards, extra cards and respec",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.perks","mobs.advice.perk_add","mobs.advice.perk_remove","mobs.advice.perk_points","mobs.advice.respec_perks"},["paragraphs"]={"These commands edit regional Origins (tier 1) and Rural Foundations (tier 2) cards, not development-tree points. Choose an owned command-target region, open Development once to load data, then mobs.perks list.","Use the listed number or a unique card key: mobs.perks add BambergSmallholders preview, then the same command without preview. This adds an extra card while retaining primary choices. Both bonuses AND penalties apply. Shared effects apply once; primary cards are not duplicated.","The vanilla card screen displays primary choices only; use mobs.perks list to inspect extras. mobs.perks remove BambergSmallholders removes one extra. mobs.perks clear removes all extras in this region while keeping primaries.","mobs.perk_points 2 restores the tier-2 choice by resetting it. mobs.respec_perks all resets normal choices. Resetting tier 1 ALSO resets tier 2 because of their dependency; settlement unlock gates remain.","Extra-card bookkeeping lives in Native/State. Preserve that folder across upgrades and back it up with your mod state. Rebuilding effects and full save/load persistence still need continued live confirmation; keep a separate untouched save."}},{["key"]="settlement",["title"]="Economy, population, livestock and families",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.treasury","mobs.advice.wealth","mobs.advice.approval","mobs.advice.grow_population","mobs.advice.animal","mobs.advice.rehouse"},["paragraphs"]={"mobs.treasury add 1000 affects your lord. mobs.wealth add 1000 affects the chosen owned region. Use set for an exact final balance. mobs.approval set 80 is bounded to 0..100 and may later be recalculated by the game. mobs.status checks targets and values.","mobs.undo only reverses the latest unchanged economy edit in this mod session. If the simulation or another action changed that value, it refuses. Inventory, spawning, construction and removal are not economy undo actions.","In the 0.16.0-alpha.3, mobs.grow_population 3 means three PEOPLE, not three families or repeated scheduled checks. Use mobs.grow_population status, then mobs.grow_population 3 preview. Apply without preview to create residents now through native family/home registration, bypassing approval and scheduled arrival days. There must be enough completed, active, non-mourning housing; homeless families take priority over new households. The date and approval are not forced, and new people have normal ongoing needs. A native refusal stops and reports the actual count without retrying. livestock_cooldown reset clears only the next-order cooldown; skip_mourning clears mourning timers without reviving residents.","mobs.animal ox 1 preview arms individual animal spawning. livestock_cooldown reset clears the next order cooldown but does not order or spawn an animal. Deer/hare individual spawning does not create registered hunting deposits.","For a person/family, hover or follow an owned unit, inspect mobs.unit, select one completed same-region house and preview mobs.rehouse selected. Capacity checks remain. mobs.skip_mourning clears active building mourning timers; it does not revive residents.","For a real hunting deposit, use mobs.spawn_wildlife deer preview or hare. Close the console and click clear owned ground. Apply without preview and click that spot again: the node and herd home are placed at your click, with animals nearby. Population is the midpoint of native normal/rich settings; rich selects its larger/native rich range. Include that site in a staffed hunting camp work area. Hunting and herd persistence in this alpha need live testing."}},{["key"]="world",["title"]="Time, weather, claims, units and command files",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.speed","mobs.advice.weather","mobs.advice.claim","mobs.advice.teleport","mobs.advice.run"},["paragraphs"]={"mobs.speed 0 pauses; mobs.speed 1 resumes. mobs.skip_day 1 preview requests native day updates, whose events may run; it is not equivalent to simulating all worker movement.","mobs.weather rain preview starts a normal weather transition when applied; instant requests immediate values. damaging applies only to rain. mobs.weather clear instant clears rain/drought immediately, but later simulation can choose new weather.","mobs.map_regions lists all map IDs. claim start requires a selected/explicit valid region, and claim finish completes a claim already belonging to you. This does not silently turn any foreign region into owned land.","mobs.follow follows a hovered unit, and mobs.follow off stops. mobs.teleport unit preview or squads preview arms a destination click. Existing orders remain active, so relocated units may move again. Hostile raiders/bandit tools create threats, not your own troops.","Command files are local text under Commands/*.txt with one exact Mobs command per line. mobs.run example.txt preview lists up to 100 commands; actual execution stops at the first error and keeps earlier completed changes. Scripts, traversal and recursive run are rejected. A batch of click tools only arms tools; it does not supply missing clicks."}},{["key"]="troubleshooting",["title"]="Diagnose, report accurately and keep upgrade state",["guides"]={"mobs.advice.version","mobs.advice.building","mobs.advice.resources","mobs.advice.refresh_resource_icons"},["paragraphs"]={"For a failure include mobs.version, game/UE4SS versions, the exact typed command, target region, selected object, expected result, actual message and whether it persists after save/reload. Attach relevant log excerpts with personal paths removed. A screenshot should include the result message and target.","Wrong target: run mobs.status, clear an unintended pin with mobs.region auto, or explicitly pin a real owned ID. Selection failure: close console and select the actual owned building first; region targeting and building selection are distinct. Native helpers refuse unsupported game layouts.","No matching deposit: surface clumps and underground reserves are separate. Use resource for clumps and deposit for reserves. Fish and eel are distinct. Search operates near the actual world position, not just a distant paper-map icon.","Alpha status is deliberate: source checks, a successful native call, a map icon and a working harvest/save-load cycle are different evidence. The bug tracker marks remaining worker/persistence reports open until reproduced and verified.","Upgrade with the game closed. Back up the old mod folder, merge the new files and retain Native/State plus your Commands files. Restart to load native helpers; Lua hot reload alone can leave an older DLL loaded. Removing the mod does not undo changes already saved. Keep an untouched save for comparison."}}}}
